Reasoning: the incumbent unconditionally uses the Steiner tree path per destination; since the evaluator sums emitted edge costs, a destination whose tree path is a detour pays extra across all `num_partitions` copies. Comparing per-dst tree-path cost vs. its cheapest unicast path and emitting the cheaper strictly dominates the incumbent (the tree path is one of the candidates), preserves validity (all hops are real directed edges of `h`, Dijkstra fallback retained), and reduces total cost whenever the 2-approximation tree misroutes any destination.
